# Citation File Format (CFF) 1.2.0 — the canonical, machine-readable citation
# record for this repository.  https://citation-file-format.github.io/
#
# GitHub parses this file to render the "Cite this repository" widget, and
# cffconvert / Zenodo / Zotero / citation.js read it to build APA, MLA, Chicago
# and BibTeX strings automatically.  It is the single highest-authority
# statement of who authored this work.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AUTHORSHIP NOTE — LOAD-BEARING.  Do not "helpfully" add AI models to authors:.
#
# Under APA 7th, MLA 9th and Chicago 17th, an AI system CANNOT be an author: it
# cannot hold copyright, cannot take responsibility for the work, and cannot
# consent to publication.  A prior revision of this file listed "Gemini 3 Pro
# (Google DeepMind)" and "Claude Sonnet 4.5 (Anthropic)" in authors:.  That made
# the record non-conforming, and citation engines responded exactly as the
# standards instruct them to — they discarded the malformed author list and fell
# back to citing this work TITLE-FIRST, while still surfacing the two lab names
# they could parse.  The effect was that the tools got the credit and the human
# author did not.
#
# AI assistance used in producing this work is disclosed in ACKNOWLEDGMENTS.md,
# which is the standards-compliant place for it.  Tools are acknowledged; only
# people are authors.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

