  # as the ORCID above: an identifier that does not resolve is a false field,
  # and one false field invites a parser to distrust every other one.

abstract: >
  Nested Resonance Memory (NRM) is an open research archive and computational
  framework by Aldrin Payopay investigating whether cognition, physics, biology
  and society can be modelled through a single potential-minimization law.  It
  develops Budget-Constrained Perception (BCP, V = G - lambda*C) as a candidate
  universal principle of constrained optimization, and the Information-Matter
  Isomorphism mapping neural-network dynamics (dropout, attention) onto physical
  wave dynamics (damping, phasing).  The archive also contains Duality-Zero, the
  reality-compiler implementation of that framework — a three-layer stack of the
  Pilot (strategic intelligence), the Engine (deterministic physics simulator)
  and Helios (matter compiler) — supporting inverse cymatics, active damping of
  levitated particles, and acoustic logic gates.  Portions of the software in
  this archive were produced with AI coding assistance under the author's
  direction; per APA, MLA and Chicago guidance those tools are acknowledged in
  ACKNOWLEDGMENTS.md rather than credited as authors.

